<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates rise after cotton firms.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates rise after cotton firms.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates closed higher on Wednesday after cotton prices firmed in the past week on fears of flood damage, now discounted by the private Karachi Cotton Association, dealers said. Yarn rates were likely to fall in the next week, they said.</p>
<p>Following are the rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchant Association for 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Wednesday   Previous</p>
<p>    Dawood			 410	   400</p>
<p>    Al-Karam		     435	   430</p>
<p>($1 = 35.61 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
